nd this happens at  a time when digitization  is is wreaking havoc in all sorts of  structures and if we do not understand  that this is not just an economic change  this is not just a change in how we  produce and live this will affect every  single institution upon which society is  based and that helps function society  and if we do not understand that we have  a collective responsibility in preparing  all these institutions to handle this  and to take and to leave no one behind  to take everyone along then we  understand how epic this challenges and  then we also understand that  disciplining ourselves along this path  to 2030 2040 2050 through a climate law  is essential to make sure we deliver on  this and to make sure that we can  correct whenever this occurs but and now  over to you  what do we put into a climate law to  what extent do we want to be  prescriptive how far will it go who are  the subject of the climate law who can  be held accountable if you have a  climate law these are all fundamental  questions where I hope you can give us  some guidance how we can best address  this again as a dad of Millennials and  Generation Z kids I understand this is  an epic challenge it's also an  incredible opportunity for Europe to  lead if we get this right I can assure  you that worldwide there will be huge  interest in studying our idea for a  climate law I get questions about this  and I had it again last week from all  parts of how you're going to do this  we'd like to see this we'd like to be  part of this so it gives Europe I think  at a unique opportunity to lead not just  within Europe but in the world  it gives again speaking ends of that new  generations and ideal again generations  that are no longer based on an  ideological vision of  world but I filled with ideals for the  future of the world it gives them an  ideal to work on the EU climate neutral  in 2050 is an ideal people love to  embrace but people will be horribly  disappointed if we do not start  delivering soon concretely on what we do  and in that context I hope the climate  law can be extremely useful and I hope  we do a good job at the Commission to  drafting the climate law that answers  your requirements it answers your hopes  and that answers your expectations of  the years to come thank you very much  good luck today thank you very much  executive vice president

